orking conditions and disrupting supply chains, resulting in delays in both deliveries and the procurement of critical components.","risk":"Acute physical climate risk to operations and supply chain"},{"note":"Long-term climate changes such as rising temperatures and sea levels may impact infrastructure integrity, logistics efficiency and the long-term viability of certain operational locations.","risk":"Chronic climate change affecting infrastructure and site viability"},{"note":"The growing need for climate adaptation and mitigation measures may divert financial resources away from strategic decarbonization initiatives, including grid expansion, renewable energy integration and investment in research and development of low carbon technologies.","risk":"Climate adaptation spend competing with growth investment"},{"note":"Exports contributed 26.19% of total turnover during the reporting period, across 70+ countries, leaving a material share of revenue exposed to overseas demand, trade and currency conditions.","risk":"Export and geographic concentration"},{"note":"The business is concentrated in electrical equipment and related projects and services - sale of products accounted for 65.67% of turnover and execution of contracts for projects and services 28.86% - serving utilities, industrial sectors, transportation, data centers and infrastructure through EPC contractors, distributors, OEMs and channel partners, so a slowdown in grid and transmission capex would transmit directly to the order book.","risk":"Customer and end-market concentration in a single activity chain"},{"note":"Hitachi Energy Ltd. is disclosed as the holding company with 71.31% of the shares, so control, technology access and group-level strategic decisions rest with the parent.","risk":"Ownership concentration in the holding company"},{"note":"The turnover rate for permanent employees rose to 9.36% in FY 2025-26 from 6.99% in FY 2024-25 (female attrition 10.63% versus 11.08%), while permanent wo